# line-length

- ID: `MD013`
- Category: Whitespace and layout
- Default: on, severity warning
- Fixable: yes
- Tags: `line_length`

Lines fit in 80 characters, with exemptions such as lone links and definitions.

## Why

Long lines are hard to work with in some editors. Diffs of short lines are also
easier to read. The exemptions are reference definitions, lines that hold only a
link or an image, and lines whose last word, such as a URL, crosses the limit.
They often cannot be split without breaking a URL.

## Options

Set them under `rules.line-length.options`.

- `max` (`integer`, default `80`): Most characters allowed on a line. 0 counts
  as 80, as in markdownlint. Also accepted as `line_length`.
- `heading_max` (`integer`, defaults to the value of `max`): Most characters
  allowed on a heading line. 0 counts as max. Also accepted as
  `heading_line_length`.
- `code_block_max` (`integer`, defaults to the value of `max`): Most characters
  allowed on a line of a code block. 0 counts as max. Also accepted as
  `code_block_line_length`.
- `ignore_code_blocks` (`boolean`, default `false`): Skip code blocks. Also
  accepted as `code_blocks`, with the opposite value.
- `ignore_tables` (`boolean`, default `false`): Skip tables. Also accepted as
  `tables`, with the opposite value.
- `ignore_headings` (`boolean`, default `false`): Skip headings. Also accepted
  as `headings`, with the opposite value.
- `ignore_urls` (`boolean`, default `false`, gomdlint only): Skip lines that
  contain a URL.
- `strict` (`boolean`, default `false`): Report every line over the limit, also
  one whose only overflow is its last word, and one that holds only a link.
- `stern` (`boolean`, default `false`): Also report a line whose only overflow
  is its last word, unless the line has no space to wrap at.
- `markdownlint_compatible` (`boolean`, default `true`, gomdlint only): Allow
  what markdownlint allows over the limit: reference definitions, lines that
  hold only a link, and a last word that starts within the limit. With false,
  every line over the limit is reported.

## Fix

The fix wraps long paragraph lines at spaces. gomdlint reports a line without a
fix when it is not paragraph text, such as a heading, a table row or code, or
when no break point is safe. gomdlint may report a finding without a fix when
the fix would change a line with one character in brackets, such as \[x\] or
\[1\], or the lines around it up to a blank line, because it could add or remove
a task list checkbox. In a document with raw HTML other than comments and plain
br, wbr, hr or img tags, gomdlint reports every finding without a fix.

## Configure

```yaml
rules:
  line-length:
    options:
      max: 80
```

Under `rules`, `line-length: false` turns the rule off and `line-length: error`
reports its findings as errors. The flag `--disable line-length` turns it off
for one run.

## Silence one line

```markdown
<!-- markdownlint-disable-next-line line-length -->
```

## markdownlint

[MD013 in markdownlint's documentation](https://github.com/DavidAnson/markdownlint/blob/v0.41.1/doc/md013.md)
